  "limitations": [
    "Primary official Aliens1986 film Bishop center-left supplies face/head/upper-body identity only. Two licensed NECA photographs support body/costume/shoes/equipment and are not actor-face authority. Exact iris tint, reverse details and unreadable tiny patch text remain unresolved; absolute1:1 fidelity is not certified.",
    "All four actual tool result archives preserve full original image_url/output_hint and submitted prompt/reference arguments; returned PNG payloads equal true hinted original PNG bytes. No other generated image or old atlas supplies identity.",
    "Sixteen genuinely distinct complete native bodies retain receding dark hair, craggy clean-shaven face, source blue coveralls/two oblique chest zips/rolled sleeves/belt/cargo pockets, anatomical RIGHT black watch and two whole white-red sneakers.",
    "S12 carries the optional source lamp in RIGHT while LEFT reaches, and S16 adds an observed RIGHT-carried source lamp despite empty-hand request. Optional carrying hand is not canonically fixed; exact requested prompts/poses and observed differences are retained.",
    "Whole connected-pose extraction with nearest satellite assignment and bounded4px weak-alpha fringe, then translations and one common nearest scale only. All alpha>12 source pixels assigned before final scale; no mirroring, limb duplication, recoloring, painting or software-generated pose.",
    "The lowest-alpha baseline is a packing measurement, not proof of physical shoe support. Intentionally raised walking/recoil feet and complete lamp/loops were visually inspected in all16 normalized poses.",
    "The new dated PNG and audit are installed without changing runtime selection. Root alone registers the correction and keeps the old atlas accessible as a variant."
